# GIMP's system preferences, which it reads before the account's own gimprc,
# so anything set in Preferences still wins. home.nix adds the lines that
# come from the theme. Every key is described in GIMP's own copy of this file:
# etc/gimp/3.0/gimprc in the package.

# No dialog at start, and no help button beside every dialog's own: F1 still
# opens GIMP's manual.
(show-welcome-dialog no)
(show-help-button no)

# More to undo than GIMP's five steps and a gigabyte an image: a step over a
# whole screenshot is about 20 MB, and what the tile cache can't hold goes
# to GIMP's swap file, not to memory. GIMP works out its threads and its
# tile cache from the machine it runs on, so those are left to it.
(undo-levels 25)
(undo-size 2G)

# The shortcuts are declared, in the shortcutsrc home.nix links into the
# account's folder, so GIMP doesn't save them as it exits. A key changed in
# Edit, Keyboard Shortcuts lasts until GIMP closes.
(save-accels no)
